jobs.description:
Are you an enthusiastic Order Picker with EPT experience, or are you eager to learn? We are looking for motivated candidates to join a modern logistics company in Helmond. As an Order Picker with EPT, you will be responsible for collecting, checking, and moving goods throughout the warehouse. Your work ensures that customer orders are processed accurately and shipped on time.

Your responsibilities:

- Picking customer orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Moving goods and pallets using an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Wrapping, labeling, and scanning pallets;
- Performing Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Supporting various warehouse and logistics processes;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the regular day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule applies:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM

- Has experience operating an EPT or is willing to learn;
- Fulltime available;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Performs well under pressure;
- Enjoys working in a team;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Has a proactive and hands-on attitude.

As an Fulltime Orderpicker at GXO in Roosendaal, you will start with a gross hourly wage of €14.99, plus shift allowances of up to 50%, meaning your hourly wage can increase to €22.49 per hour. This makes working as an Order Picker / Warehouse EMployee especially attractive! Yoy also receive travel expernse reimbursement of € 0.25 per kilometer.

In this role, you will pick and check orders, prepare them for shipment and make sure everything leaves the warehouse on time. You will work with an English voice-picking system and an electric pallet truck (EPT).

Every day, you will start together with your team during the daily briefing in Roosendaal, conveniently located near Breda, Etten-Leur and Bergen op Zoom. After that, you will get to work: picking orders, wrapping and packing goods, unloading containers and stacking pallets. You will accurately process everything you do in the WMS system.

You will work in a two-shift system:

- 06:00 – 14:45
- 14:45 – 23:30

You can work full-time (40 hours) or part-time (from 32 hours). You are also available to work an average of 2 Saturdays per month.

